        topic: "Mixed",
        fp: "Defendant wanted to break into an office building at night to steal computer equipment[cite: 41]. Defendant walked into the building during regular business hours at 3:00 PM when the lobby was open to the public, took an elevator to the fourth floor, and hid inside an uncarpeted mechanical boiler room[cite: 41]. Defendant remained inside the boiler room until 11:00 PM, well after the building had closed to the public, all exterior doors had been locked, and all employees had departed[cite: 41]. At 11:00 PM, Defendant pushed open the closed, unlatched metal door of the boiler room, stepped out into the darkened fourth-floor hallway, and walked toward the corporate accounting suite[cite: 41]. However, before Defendant could reach the accounting suite, an armed night security guard rounding the corner spotted Defendant's flashlight and detained him at gunpoint[cite: 41]. The jurisdiction adheres to traditional common law criminal definitions[cite: 41].",
